{"chunk_id": "a192c0d98b08", "text": "Maricha warns Ravana that Rama\u2019s power is so terrifying that even hearing syllables beginning with \u201cRa\u201d fills him with dread, and he predicts disaster if Ravana provokes him. He argues that Rama has already slain mighty demons like Khara and that opposing him will doom the titans. Ravana, enraged, dismisses the counsel and insists on his plan to abduct Sita. He rebukes Maricha for speaking pessimistically and lectures him on obedience to kings, whom he likens to divine powers. Ravana then reveals his scheme: Maricha must transform into a wondrous golden deer to lure Rama away from the hermitage. When Rama pursues it and Lakshmana is drawn away by a deceptive cry, Ravana will seize Sita and carry her to Lanka. The passage marks the decisive plotting that sets the famous abduction in motion.\nRavana angrily rejects Maricha\u2019s warning about Rama and orders him to become a golden deer to lure Rama away so Ravana can abduct Sita.\nThemes: hubris, ignored counsel, deception plot, abduction scheme, fate and downfall", "vector": [-0.0017954210052266717, -0.012396152131259441, 0.0036009475588798523, -0.008145080879330635, -0.018971502780914307, 0.009236481040716171, -0.044814784079790115, -0.027675757184624672, -0.02170674130320549, -0.02127557061612606, 0.02419944480061531, 0.006420398596674204, 0.004749612882733345, 0.016411427408456802, -0.015805093571543694, -0.003631264204159379, 0.04470699280500412, -0.006966098677366972, 0.022191807627677917, -0.021854955703020096, 0.006225024349987507, -0.00511678121984005, -0.00198237388394773, -0.002435439731925726, -0.03357740491628647, 0.005322260782122612, 0.01864812523126602, -0.0392904132604599, 0.0038199012633413076, -0.018324747681617737, -0.00801707711070776, -0.02437460795044899, 0.01711208000779152, -0.013837878592312336, -0.03090953640639782, -0.009074792265892029, 0.015845516696572304, -0.01517181284725666, 0.014888856559991837, -0.011580970138311386, -0.002470809